# decisionledger.allow -- why each file still writes the graph in Python (0.0.23 K).
#   keep FILE CATEGORY reason   (CATEGORY: test-tool | generic-assembly | pending-migration | cdx-pending)
#   allowop OP MANIFEST STEM reason   (one transitional manifest row, matched by stem)
#   rise STAGE reason           (a reviewed increase; none today)
# Owner rule: "the target column cannot come from a fact" is NOT a reason -- parameterised templates
# (exec/finite_rules.py install_template) express fact-generated control; a keep line must say why
# even a template cannot.  pending-migration lines are debts of 0.0.23 K, not accepted residue.
# Also not a migration: Python computing the transitions (state, byte -> target, actions) and a template
# merely re-emitting them as "facts".  Template facts must be domain facts (types, prefixes, recipes,
# character classes); the control structure itself has to be written in the table.
keep enc/shacheck.py test-tool check script probe graph (1 sites)
keep parse/gen.py pending-migration the generic P core moved to exec/build/procs.py and G to exec/build/graph.py; left: 1 site in the pipeline helpers until parse/gen.py helpers become manifests
keep parse2/diagnosticcheck.py test-tool builds a probe graph inside the check script; never part of a product construction (8 sites)
